hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1114","Bundar told us, Ishaq bin Yusuf Al-Azraq told us, Al-Jariri told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prays four rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer. He does not miss them. She said: And he used to say: “Nice two surahs.” They are recited in two rak’ahs before dawn: “Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’” and “Say, ‘O you disbelievers.”"
